title: Proposition 108
---
order: 108
---
short_label: X.108
---
sections:

#### prop_section ####
kind: proposition
----
statement: If from a rational area a medial area is subtracted, the side of the remaining area becomes one of two irrational straight lines, either an apotome or a minor straight line.
----
proof:

Let the medial area {BD} be subtracted from the rational area {BC|BCf}.

I say that the side of the remainder {EC} becomes one of two irrational straight lines, either an apotome or a minor straight line.

Set out a rational straight line {FG}, to {FG} apply the rectangular parallelogram {GH|GHf} equal to {BC|BCf}, and subtract {GK} equal to {DB}. Then the remainder {EC} equals {LH}.

Since, then, {BC|BCf} is rational, and {BD} medial, while {BC|BCf} equals {GH|GHf}, and {BD} equals {GK}, therefore {GH|GHf} is rational, and {GK} is medial.

<figure class="diagram">
<canvas id="canvas_0" width="280" height="240" tabindex="0"></canvas>
<noscript><img alt="X.108 diagram" src="propX108.gif"/></noscript>
<script type="text/javascript">
    // Joyce's figure: the rational area BC (ABC and its fourth corner) with
